Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:34:47-07:00","id":1382539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382491#post1382491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a consequence of some Awakening, when your Trials rewrite the fallen world.<br /> The Pc remember only their &quot;original reality&quot;, but they are the only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe what people think to know about this story is heavily distorted by the imperial workings and aponoias performed by jesus after he became archmage (and by his ascension if he reached it).<br /> It would explain how a poor man without powerful politic allies could have estabilished one of the more successful religion in the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 04-19-2020, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T11:00:03-07:00","id":1382556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382539#post1382539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe what people think to know about this story is heavily distorted by the imperial workings and aponoias performed by jesus after he became archmage (and by his ascension if he reached it).<br /> It would explain how a poor man without powerful politic allies could have estabilished one of the more successful religion in the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:02:20-07:00","id":1382577,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T23:21:44-07:00","id":1382684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382482#post1382482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know what the words Intercession and Boundaries mean or how they relate to the Thyrsus (plus I think Jesus is more of an ascetic monk than a shaman), but I like the rest of your ideas. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intercession and Boundaries are the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/pathfinding/\" target=\"_blank\">two keywords</a> that define the Thyrsus Path.<br /> <br /> In many shamanistic traditions, a key part of the job description is to mediate between the spirit world and the mortal world. This is something that influenced Werewolf stuff. If you've watched the cartoon Avatar: the Last Airbender, they talk about the Avatar's responsibility as such a mediator fairly early on in season 1.<br /> <br /> Boundaries is about keeping what belongs in one world in that world. Intercession is about speaking on behalf of others to restore harmony and keep things better. A shaman intercesses on behalf of a spirit to tell people to stop doing spirit-harming things like deforestation or pollution. A shaman intercesses on behalf of a human to keep meddlesome spirits from screwing around with people's lives for spirit reasons. It's a job not dissimilar to that of a hostage negotiator.<br /> <br /> Intercession is also the term that Catholics use to describe how most instances of prayer actually works. The reason that Catholics offer dedications to saints is that the expectation is that those Saints are in heaven and can speak with God on behalf of the petitioner. (I'm not and did not grow up Catholic, so I might be getting this wrong.) More powerfully and more generally in terms of Christian belief as a whole, it is believed that the act of Jesus' sacrifice was specifically an act of intercession: Jesus stood in the way of God's judgment upon mankind as intercessor and took it upon himself instead. (<a href=\"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/08070a.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Catholic Encyclopedia</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercession_of_saints\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a>)<br /> <br /> Redefining Boundaries was also a lot of what Jesus himself spent his time doing. Moneylenders, lepers, prostitutes, hell, even Samaritans: the boundary between them and the Jews is false and should be erased. Moneylenders in the Temple? An inappropriate transgression across a boundary that he'll angrily enforce.<br /> <br /> Framing this in Mage terms, it's not hard to see Jesus as someone who foresaw a bad thing coming and stopped it from happening by building a big ritual and using himself as the only available power source, and struggling to use the few years he had available to him before that to build a better world for the people around him. If you want to throw in Imperial Mysteries, it's entirely possible that his short lifetime was because he ended up screwing around with the timeline for some reason that distorted things so that he was remembered for having no grandparents and also prodigious at a curiously young age: like, maybe he had to squeeze time together to erase a pandemic in Jerusalem or something so a thing he did in his 40s actually happened when he was 12.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382482#post1382482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I did that cause I like crossovers. I mean, if this was real life, mages wouldn\u2019t just hang out with mages and vampires with vampires. You know what I mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's hanging out, and then there's explaining an entire clan of vampires being based off one guy having stabbed a random mage this one time. What was so special about this boy's blood that coating a spear with it turns the bearer into a vampire progenitor? Crossover without purpose is like mixing paints together because the original colors looked nice. It's possible to get something interesting, but usually it's just a spot of mud.<br /> <br /> There are excellent stories to tell about vampires and mages fucking and fighting and finagling, and Dark Eras and Contagion Chronicles both do a good job of setting up ideas for them. It's even possible and laudable to tell stories about Jesus that involve them. I... hope you do that at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:38:33-07:00","id":1382721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. This is really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:42:24-07:00","id":1382723,"title":"","content":"But the book actually says that the Lancea et Sanctum (Covenant, not clan) is based off of Longinus stabbing Jesus in the side with his spear. The word Lancea even means \u201cspear\u201d in Latin. I just explained the story by making Jesus a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:37:06-07:00","id":1382749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382723#post1382723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the book actually says that the Lancea et Sanctum (Covenant, not clan) is based off of Longinus stabbing Jesus in the side with his spear. The word Lancea even means \u201cspear\u201d in Latin. I just explained the story by making Jesus a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't explain anything. In fact, it raises even more questions about why all those things happened to Longinus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:21:31-07:00","id":1382788,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> because he stabbed Jesus in the side with a spear. It\u2019s in the Testament of Longinus, which is like actually an official sourcebook published by the company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:26:26-07:00","id":1382789,"title":"","content":"It literally says something like \u201cBecause you stabbed this man with your spear while he hung on the cross, you are being cursed with [undeath].\u201d Which is basically flowery language saying that some mysterious entity has transformed Longinus into a revenant (much like Dracula many years later, except Dracula was actually Embraced).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:28:30-07:00","id":1382791,"title":"","content":"At least this thread got a lot of responses...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:35:39-07:00","id":1382793,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> oh wait a minute. You\u2019re asking why him being a mage is connected to Longinus becoming a revenant. Because the being who cursed Longinus was the Archangel Gabriel, a Supernal entity from the Aether who was Jesus\u2019s patron.<br /> <br /> Why did Gabriel do that? Idk. Abrahamic beings have weird ideas about how to punish people, and one of them is turning the person into a vampire (like Caine in World of Darkness). Not sure how much of a punishment that is, but Angels think differently than humans.<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. That really clarifies things for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T21:16:37-07:00","id":1384099,"title":"","content":"I'll put a disclaimer that I'm speaking as an atheist right now who don't believe that Jesus possessed any supernatural powers (and in my opinion, he is more interesting that way), so if that disqualifies anything you don't need to read further.<br /> <br /> If I were you I would focus on what importance Jesus would have for your players in their story, since I assume this is for your game sessions and I believe that everything should be from the perspective of your players. I say that because I'm sure that lots and lots of things we've heard about Jesus are the result of hearsay, rumours, propaganda and elaborate theology, the grand majority of it written and propagated by other people long after his death. The bible for example was not compiled until some two centuries after his death and has often been changed, revised and many things are altered in translation. Was he a charismatic prophet and cult leader? Yes. Did he do all of the fantastic miracles and feats attributed to him? I'd say it's more reasonable that these were fiction to glorify and justify the new official religion of the Roman Empire and, later, the Catholic Church. We would know very little about the real man underneath all the centuries of religious dogma and writing.<br /> <br /> In your game world, Jesus could very well have been some kind of supernatural being, but the real truth of him should be elusive at best. as they keep digging and nagging into the mystery of Jesus they start running into layer upon layer of propaganda and misinformation. In the game world of CofD there are not only many religious leaders and institutions who would want to appropriate Jesus and propagate their own views of him, but tons of supernatural factions as well. The Lancea et Sanctum come to mind as lorekeepers of real, original sources from Jesus (or maybe not, they just claim to have those to gain legitimacy). I can imagine many mages as well being involved, both those who would use the myriad of variations of Christianity and Jesus as the light to guide sleepers to awaken as well as those using these as an elaborate labyrinth to avert nosy sleepers from knowing about real magic, or those who use Christianity to build their own cults in a powergame.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T00:49:23-07:00","id":1384120,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a> Thank you. I really like your ideas. I\u2019m not Christian either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:14:55-07:00","id":1384396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1384120#post1384120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Thank you. I really like your ideas. I\u2019m not Christian either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said you are Wiccan though. Does that entail a belief in the supernatural? (not critizicing you, just genuinely curious)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:28:35-07:00","id":1384399,"title":"","content":"It does. I believe in a Goddess and I believe that magick works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:00:40-07:00","id":1385439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382793#post1382793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a Supernal entity from the Aether</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1382793#post1382793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abrahamic beings</div> </div> </div> </div>I uhh...I don't understand why we're conflating these two things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:07:59-07:00","id":1385480,"title":"","content":"@Inodiv I always assumed they were the same. (Is that what conflate means?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:08:29-07:00","id":1385481,"title":"","content":"@Inodiv ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:11:10-07:00","id":1385483,"title":"","content":"Well, technically I always assumed that the Abrahamic angels were actually Supernal beings from the Aether.<br /> <br /> You guys did NOT like this one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:12:42-07:00","id":1385496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1385483#post1385483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, technically I always assumed that the Abrahamic angels were actually Supernal beings from the Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal beings from the Aether are symbol-creatures corresponding to the Arcana of Forces and Prime, i.e. descriptive processes for physical and magical power, often possessed of a strong affinity for codes of honor, purity, wisdom, etc. They largely exist outside of direct reference to existing mortal belief structures' mythology, because the manifestations of divine power recognized unambiguously as &quot;Supernal beings&quot; are either magical constructs assembled by Awakened summoners or are the denizens of parallel worlds that come into alignment with the rest of experienced reality through rare and esoteric confluences that have a greater impact on their surroundings; in neither case are they generally given to wandering beyond the safety of their established boundaries.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu and their indwelling temakhs from Mummy: the Curse are substantially closer to the sort of &quot;Abrahamic angels&quot; that would mesh well with a Longinus-era Vampire story, being corrupted pure-magic servants of the awful manifestations of primordial Law whose sorcery had a distinctly Biblical bent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:54:34-07:00","id":1385573,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I like that. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T13:21:17-07:00","id":1391535,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Michael;n1382124 Also, to go back to what GibbeeringEloquence said, being a mage seems to have nothing really to do with being the founding figure of a religion.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Not exactly, if you've read &quot;Jesus the Magician&quot; by Morton Smith or &quot;Magic in the New Testament&quot; by Robert Conner you will know that Jesus's actions were very much in keeping with the behavior of other contemporary magicians. Jesus was so good at it that other magicians Jewish, Pagan, and God-Fearer (proto-Christian), would exorcise in his name even while he was still alive. Remember also that Jesus was executed for necromancy i.e. raising Lazarus from the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","user":"moonwolf8","date":". 05-25-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T15:19:55-07:00","id":1402306,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading &quot;Jesus The Sorcerer&quot; by Robert Conner yesterday and was reminded of Lazarus. How does Lazarus fit in the Chronicles of Darkness? Is he a Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T15:35:24-07:00","id":1402311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402306#post1402306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished reading &amp;quot;Jesus The Sorcerer&amp;quot; by Robert Conner yesterday and was reminded of Lazarus. How does Lazarus fit in the Chronicles of Darkness? Is he a Mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>However you want him to. Though I think you may need to do some narrative stretching for him to be a Mummy, as Jesus only knew him when he was dead, so he wouldn't be a cultist. Alternatively he is just a man who was resurrected. Some splats, including the Malleus Maleficarum, can resurrect people.<br /> <br /> But again, whatever you want him to be. I would just keep in mind that if you plan on playing with this aspect, talk with any of your christian players (if you have any) if they would be fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T13:42:25-07:00","id":1402454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1391535#post1391535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly, if you've read &quot;Jesus the Magician&quot; by Morton Smith or &quot;Magic in the New Testament&quot; by Robert Conner you will know that Jesus's actions were very much in keeping with the behavior of other contemporary magicians. Jesus was so good at it that other magicians Jewish, Pagan, and God-Fearer (proto-Christian), would exorcise in his name even while he was still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you're talking about the real Jesus there. I was talking about Penelope's version. Like, the two parts of their story didn't fit together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember also that Jesus was executed for necromancy i.e. raising Lazarus from the dead. </div> </div> </div>I'm not a historian of Christianity but I'm not aware of any evidence of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T14:30:27-07:00","id":1402469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402454#post1402454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you're talking about the real Jesus there. I was talking about Penelope's version. Like, the two parts of their story didn't fit together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not a historian of Christianity but I'm not aware of any evidence of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, Jesus was officially executed for Treason by Pontius Pilate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T15:12:27-07:00","id":1402480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402469#post1402469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, Jesus was officially executed for Treason by Pontius Pilate</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, I believe the implication of the gospels is that he had the book thrown at him. Using magic might well come under that (As I remember, the Romans were never terribly happy with Judaism anyway); but I have a hard time believing that he'd be tried for bringing some guy back from the dead... Unless you accept a theological view of Jesus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":"07-12-2020, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T18:34:21-07:00","id":1402506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402469#post1402469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last time I checked, Jesus was officially executed for Treason by Pontius Pilate</div> </div> </div> </div>He was executed for treason.<br /> <br /> And I gave up on my idea. It just didn\u2019t fit together the way I thought it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T20:38:37-07:00","id":1402518,"title":"","content":"I haven't read this whole thing cuz it looks like its turning into a project, so, I'll just toss my two bits in *blindly*.<br /> <br /> My advice is that, if you have ANY MAGE CONTENT... consider <i>The Exarchs.</i> Particularly The Father. Now keep in mind The Father's obsession is the tyranny of dogma and religious authority. This means The Father has a huge stake in this. So does the Prophet, Exarch of Time.<br /> <br /> Words of Truth and Time magic <i>should not work</i> in regards to anything to do with Jesus or other <i>sensitive topics</i> regarding other people's major beliefs... not just because that's good taste, it is because The Father and The Prophet want to <i>maximize</i> the Lie and authority they soak up from the proliferation of their symbols. This means that The Father <i>prefers</i> blind faith over Truth, not 100% so, but enough that The Father clearly benefits from keeping any information about Jesus under a dense forest of obfuscation, along with other martyrs. When even <i>Mages</i> must fight over faith, as the Seers clearly do... then The Father is pleased. And how to make sure no Sleeper thinks that they matter in the analogues of history than to make sure the person who many believe was the greatest among mankind with no sin? Hide Jesus, but let his history survive the ages (pending &quot;tasteful&quot; edits by historians), you cannot escape his legacy and yet you cannot prove what isn't already written...<br /> <br /> This could include the prophet Muhammad, the Buddha Gautama, and other belief-sensitive peoples. If any religion has Supernal symbols in it, the Exarchs <i>half to hide it!</i> It maximizes their tyrannic potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T20:46:54-07:00","id":1402519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402518#post1402518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read this whole thing cuz it looks like its turning into a project, so, I'll just toss my two bits in *blindly*.<br /> <br /> My advice is that, if you have ANY MAGE CONTENT... consider <i>The Exarchs.</i> Particularly The Father. Now keep in mind The Father's obsession is the tyranny of dogma and religious authority. This means The Father has a huge stake in this. So does the Prophet, Exarch of Time.<br /> <br /> Words of Truth and Time magic <i>should not work</i> in regards to anything to do with Jesus or other <i>sensitive topics</i> regarding other people's major beliefs... not just because that's good taste, it is because The Father and The Prophet want to <i>maximize</i> the Lie and authority they soak up from the proliferation of their symbols. This means that The Father <i>prefers</i> blind faith over Truth, not 100% so, but enough that The Father clearly benefits from keeping any information about Jesus under a dense forest of obfuscation, along with other martyrs. When even <i>Mages</i> must fight over faith, as the Seers clearly do... then The Father is pleased. And how to make sure no Sleeper thinks that they matter in the analogues of history than to make sure the person who many believe was the greatest among mankind with no sin? Hide Jesus, but let his history survive the ages (pending &amp;quot;tasteful&amp;quot; edits by historians), you cannot escape his legacy and yet you cannot prove what isn't already written...<br /> <br /> This could include the prophet Muhammad, the Buddha Gautama, and other belief-sensitive peoples. If any religion has Supernal symbols in it, the Exarchs <i>half to hide it!</i> It maximizes their tyrannic potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, as a catholic, I think it's fine to experiment with the idea, but I agree with the overall assessment. Besides making sure everyone at the table is fine with it, when asking for help online, I would recommend being careful. Topics such as these can easily be misunderstood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T21:04:01-07:00","id":1402520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382092-the-life-of-jesus-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1402518#post1402518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Truth and Time magic <i>should not work</i> in regards to anything to do with Jesus or other <i>sensitive topics</i> regarding other people's major beliefs...</div> </div> </div> </div>Words of Truth specifically only works on things that are both objectively true and known by the speaker to be true. Time magic requires appropriate sympathetic connections and Yantras to work on anything that didn't happen basically yesterday. I appreciate the appeal to cultural sensitivity, but there's no need to make faith-pertinent history arbitrarily impossible to address with magic when it's already not easy to examine most pieces of history old enough to have branches of archaeology dedicated to them and there's no need to say anything about how a spell that conveys known factual information as truthful interacts with faith-based statements.<br /> <br /> Centuries are long. That's plenty of obfuscation for most magical purposes.","